WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.360
Phantom Fighter!

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:08.560
Wild Chinese phantoms, Kyonshi's, are on the loose, wreaking havoc on eight villages!

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:32.920
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:33.940
I'm Mike.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.200
I'm Sean.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:42.920
And I'm Joe. You would not know this, it would be impossible to know this, but Phantom Fighter is one of

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.520
those movie tie-in video games.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.940
Oh my god, really?

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.160
But not for a movie released in America.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.920
Well, I figured that.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.780
Yes. It is based on the 1985 Hong Kong movie, Mr.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.680
Vampire. Wow.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Because of all the vampires in this game.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.720
Well, yeah, that makes sense, because I had...

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.360
I had such a different reaction.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.980
I wouldn't have thought that this was a part of any kind of mainstream media.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:18.620
Right, right. Well, the movie must have taken them a long time to make because they had to keep giving

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:21.260
the actors time to just hop everywhere.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:26.340
Um... That's a reference to the fact that all the enemies just hop.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.820
They don't walk.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.000
They don't really do anything else.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.440
They just hop at you.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.860
Yeah. I think they doubled down on hopping to be the next big thing that kids were going to

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.100
love. I mean, it seems spooky.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:44.800
Maybe that's what Keonchis are known for, but I don't know anything about these Chinese

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.520
phantoms. Do you guys have any...

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.380
No. ...masters in Chinese folklore?

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.060
Not that I remember, no.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:56.160
I just want to say, like, I didn't read the manual.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.920
I didn't know that there was a movie.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:05.020
Um... I don't even think that it's mentioned on, like, the little stub of a Wikipedia article

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:05.960
there is for this game.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.420
But I thought that this was just a piece of, like, outsider art.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.820
Like, the...

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.420
The... All... Just completely insulated from any...

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.300
Uh... Any, like, trends in the gaming space at this time.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:25.700
Uh... Really not knowing the rules about how things are supposed to go in games like these.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.940
It... The whole...

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.600
The concept of the enemies and how they acted.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.100
And you have, like, a sidekick, and I'm not sure who he's supposed to be.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.920
I don't know who you're supposed to be.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:42.400
If you're supposed to be, like, a Sherlock kind of guy with the long, like, jacket that

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.680
also knows karate.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.200
I... There were so many questions that I had about this game that I guess I could have looked

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.640
up. You gotta watch the movie.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.000
I gotta watch the movie, I guess, now.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.420
Yeah, you're like the ninth doctor.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.840
Yeah. The war doctor, now.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.220
Yeah, I thought it was weird, too, because...

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:04.600
Oh, usually when you see a movie tie-in game, usually, not always, it's...

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:05.740
It plays it safe.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:09.200
It, like, it uses a formula, a tried-and-true formula.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:14.720
This, for better or for worse, is being, like, ambitious in trying to do, like, its own thing,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.300
where it's, like, it's got that kind of Prince of Persia-style control, where you, like, pressing

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:23.740
forward starts, like, a whole, like, animation loop, and it's got this, like...

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:29.100
You're doing this, like, side-scroller on what apparently is, I guess, an overworld map,

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:33.860
and then you go into, like, buildings with little sort of mini boss battles, and then

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.940
leave. It's, like...

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:39.460
It's not like any game we've ever played before, which is kind of interesting for our

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:44.160
movie tie-in. I mean, I guess we had Ghostbusters, which also really, like, made up its own rules.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.440
And Jaws. And Jaws, that's true.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:51.800
Good point. But, like, I guess maybe I'm more conditioned to this from, like, games that I grew up with,

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.980
but, like, I'm used to, like, movie tie-in games in, like, the 90s and 2000s being, like,

00:03:56.540 --> 00:04:01.280
kind of, like, the most generic gameplay with, like, a movie tie-in skin over it.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:07.560
Yeah. And it's interesting, though, that because I didn't know that this was a movie tie-in at

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.820
all, so this is even...

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:13.600
These aren't even the thoughts that I was having coming into this discussion.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:19.520
Sean, you're not wrong, though, that it is kind of, like, weirdly made in a vacuum because

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:22.980
the developer, MarioNet, um, is...

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:26.700
has never made an NES game before, and I don't know if

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:32.320
they'll make another one. In my current list of, like, games we're gonna be playing up until 1991, they're not listed

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:38.100
again. The publisher is FCI, and we've played some interesting games from them in the past, but

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:42.020
the developer is just kind of, like, is it weird?

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:45.320
Were they just, like, yeah, it'd be neat to make a game based off this movie that came

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.380
out five years ago?

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:51.080
Was he... What was he developing before, or is this the first time we've seen his name ever?

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.140
Uh, MarioNet's not a person.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.280
Um, it's a company, but I...

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:56.440
No, he knows Vic Takai.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.580
Oh, yeah, gotcha.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:01.860
Um, I could not tell you, because when you search for MarioNet, you're not gonna get the

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:02.920
video game developer.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.220
You're gonna get the puppets.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.920
Marionette. Okay, I thought you were saying a person's name, MarioNet.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.260
That's what I thought you were saying, too.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.180
Oh, I gotcha, that's funny.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.420
Marionette. Yeah. It's Marionette.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:20.760
Does that make you feel better?

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:21.960
It makes you feel better.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:28.820
I don't know if the tone of the game gave this off or whatever, but the manual has, like,

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:33.300
clearly this game was, especially if that's referencing a Hong Kong movie that none of us knew,

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:38.480
like, it was made on the Famicom and then, like, came over, and the guys who, like, made

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:43.600
the manual for the North American audience, the story has, like, a completely different

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.940
tone in this manual.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:49.360
It starts with, those wacky Chinese phantoms are on the loose again.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:53.760
It's like, I did not get that vibe from the game at all.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:01.840
Like, the game has, like, people giving you, like, you know, a lot of story details and,

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:06.620
like, you know, like, explaining the Keon Cheese and then it's just like, dang it, like, you

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:09.920
know, those wacky Chinese phantoms escape Chinese jail.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.220
It's like, stop it.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:12.660
It's not what happened.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.420
Well, you know, I mean, the wacky part, like, one of you guys said earlier, like, oh, they

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:18.960
are kind of spooky the way they hop.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.000
I couldn't disagree more.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.200
They're very ridiculous looking.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.180
That was a joke.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:29.000
But, like, they're so silly looking.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:34.500
They just, they hop with their arms out, like, like, you would think, like, a cartoon zombie.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.200
Arms out, they hop around, like, I don't know.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.840
Well, I don't think of a cartoon zombie hopping anywhere.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:46.920
I guess the only way that it can be spooky is just that it's very uncanny valley, in a way.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:51.880
I mean, which is, it's, you can't do, like, an NES uncanny valley because it's so far

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.680
outside of the valley in one direction.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.360
But, you know what I mean.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.440
It's like, they're acting weird.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:03.580
Yeah. It's also spooky in the, like, in the, like, realistic sense where it's like, something's

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:07.640
not scary to look at, but it's, like, scary because of how it can, you know, like, ever

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.780
play, um, oh, what is it called?

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:14.520
Perfection. The board game Perfection that you put all the pieces in before it pops up.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.040
Yeah. Like, that's not scary.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:18.660
Yeah, you have to put in different shapes, right?

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:23.900
Yeah, yeah. That's not scary inherently, but it is, like, it does have this, like, scariness because

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:24.940
you're, like, there's anxiety.

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:30.100
And I guess if I'm trying to stretch what would make this scary is, like, I have some anxiety

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:34.060
about the fact that I have no idea when I'm going to take damage or not.

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:38.980
Like, if my kick is going to land or if their weird outstretched hands are just going to

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:41.840
somehow hurt me. And, like, that gives me some anxiety.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:46.040
I'm like, I gotta be, play it really safe, but it's not, like, not the traditional.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.100
That's just playing a video game.

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:53.220
It is, but it's, like, it's, like, more so, I guess, because it's, like, I don't feel like

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.940
I have that much control over it.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:59.520
Or at least I don't understand in what way I have control over when I'm taking damage.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.340
In some instances that I'm, like, I don't know.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:05.700
I'm really trying to stretch what could be spooky about this game.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:06.940
So, bear with me.

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:13.160
But, yeah, like, I guess it's just the anxiety of, like, not knowing how to actually avoid.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:16.060
Like, sometimes when I do this, my kick lands.

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.000
Other times I get hit.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.540
That's spooky. I don't know.

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.020
Someone else talk. Yeah.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:26.840
Yeah, I could talk because what's funny is, you know, going back to just the story or the

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:32.500
plot or whatever, you know, they are setting out to be an ambitious, story-driven game in

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:37.580
the sense that it's a side-scrolling action game where you have to go to eight villages.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.480
It's not an open world in that sense.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:40.680
You start at Village 1.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.920
You have to do everything in Village 1 to move over to Village 2.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.540
And, yes, they really are just called Village 1, Village 2.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:51.160
They could have probably given them names to make them feel more lived in, but whatever.

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:56.940
And then inside that village, like, you're free to roam around and visit, like, you know,

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:00.780
houses, temples, graveyards, the school.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.840
And, you know, do that in any order you please.

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:07.600
And, obviously, like, there's probably a good order or whatever.

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:11.420
But it's not really, like, it's not a life simulator in that regard.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.220
You're there. No, it's just nonlinear.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:17.620
Right. You're just there to take out these kionchis that you have to find.

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:19.900
And they're not hard to find.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.500
It's not like you're, like, where are these damn fandoms?

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:23.480
Like, they're everywhere. Don't worry.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:27.420
And once you take them all out, then you can move to the next village.

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:32.880
But along the way, there's a lot of, like, story-driven stuff going on from both the people

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:38.300
that you run into giving you, like, information that doesn't feel like it's necessary.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.600
But then you find out you're going to be quizzed on it by the guards.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:42.780
And that's not great.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:48.460
Or there's, like, information that you might need to know how to, like, do new moves or,

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.780
you know, deal with a certain enemy.

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:56.460
And that's why I'm making my first recommendation for anybody who even tries to check out this game.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.880
Don't do what I did and start Phantom Fighter at the fastest tech speed.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:02.840
Because it does let you choose your tech speed.

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:05.640
But fast is... It's the first thing it lets you choose.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:10.800
Right. And fast is for those who don't care at all about the plot or have memorized it.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:16.140
Because it just scrolls right through it so fast that you just get the very last thing

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:18.040
before you push the A button to continue.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:21.000
You don't even get a chance to read what happens next.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.860
One thing, you mentioned the quizzing.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:28.020
And I imagine you mean, like, getting to a part in the game that I did not,

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:32.080
where it actually quizzes you on things about the game itself.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:38.900
But I, like, you know, you go to actually learn these moves.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:43.060
You have to go to places where they will ask you trivia questions.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:46.100
But it's just general trivia, like, in our world.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:50.720
Like, a question that I was asked in order to then learn a move was,

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.360
who created Ultima?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.880
And I'm like, okay, in a vacuum, that...

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.660
Okay, maybe Ultima is also a thing in this game's world.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.600
And, like, it's the name of, like, a wizard.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:02.060
It's like, no, it's just Lord British.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.380
Like, that is the answer.

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:07.000
Or, like, how many states are there on the American...

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.860
How many stars are on the American flag?

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:11.220
Like, oh, there's just answers in the real world.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:15.000
It's a very strange, like, fourth wall break there.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.880
Yeah. Yeah, and I wonder if that, like...

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:20.080
Does that tie into the movie somehow?

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.040
Yeah, they're, like, weird, like...

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.580
Is bar trivia a part of it?

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:28.740
Contemporary trivia, yeah. But that was very weird to me, too.

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:31.660
Because when, you know, what you were describing, Mike, like,

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:37.000
at least there's, like, stuff you can pay attention to in-game to get it.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:38.160
But this is just, like...

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:41.480
I wasn't told when I played this that I'd have to have, like,

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:44.220
historical knowledge, you know?

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.560
So, like, that is...

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:47.800
So, when I got the Ultima thing, I thought at first,

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.860
until I, like, read the options, I guess,

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:54.600
that, like, that was some piece of lore that I missed.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:12:01.580
Because Ultima is often used in games or stories.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.680
Square games, yeah. Yeah, square games specifically.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:05.040
Anyone play Final Fantasy XVI?

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:11.180
But the... So, I was, like, wondering what, you know, what that was all about.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:16.160
But then, also, just to back up a little bit to what you were saying, Mike,

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:17.280
about how you can kind of...

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:24.640
How you have to visit and take out each of these phantoms in order to progress.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:27.040
But you can go in any order.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.500
It felt like they missed out on a little bit of, like...

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.880
I feel like there's two reasons to do this.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:34.740
And maybe there are more, but there's two that I can think of.

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:43.940
Where letting you go out of order and having significant differences in your play style

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:47.060
because you went out of order is one reason.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.580
Or the other reason is, like...

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.960
You can skip over these things.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:55.200
Like, that's what... You can skip over these things, but then when you get to the end of the level,

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:56.140
you just can't progress.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:00.920
So, the only reason I can see wanting to skip over something is if it's, like...

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:03.000
Again, a risk-reward thing where it's, like...

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:06.440
If you skip over it, you might miss out on a power-up that'll help you later.

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:07.600
But, like, it doesn't matter.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.820
You have to go back and do it later.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:13.020
So, I don't really get why they made it, like...

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.620
Optional to go into each of these areas to fight each of these bosses.

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.960
If, like, once you get through, like, the 25 of them in the first level...

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:23.160
And if you skipped one, it's just gonna be like,

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.920
Well, you can't move on until you go back and do that one.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:28.460
Like, I don't feel like there was incentive to change it up.

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:32.540
So, in a purely mechanical sense, you're right.

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:35.060
There is no reason for them to do it this way.

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:38.200
But, I guess, in a storytelling...

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.720
Or, I guess, in an immersion sense...

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:44.580
Like, it does make sense to have it be houses you have to go into.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:48.020
And there's, like, a hub area that...

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:50.980
Just to give it more of a sense of place.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.640
And maybe that sense of place is very important to the movie.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:56.680
I don't know. That's grasping...

00:13:56.680 --> 00:14:01.280
But there's at least, like, the narrative aspect to it, too.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.360
Yeah. I mean, definitely, there's the narrative aspect.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.340
But I guess it's just...

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:10.700
Why could... The narrative aspect would be the same if I could not skip a level.

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.000
If you want to call it a level.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.300
